WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.881
Adding more grouping columns makes the summary more
detailed Here we group

00:00:05.894 --> 00:00:12.213
by patient and diagnosis together One output row now
represents one patient-and-diagnosis

00:00:12.226 --> 00:00:18.584
combination Run the example and compare it with the
previous one-row-per-diagnosis

00:00:18.611 --> 00:00:23.245
query You should see more rows because the grain is
more specific

00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:29.515
This is an important design choice If the question
asks how many

00:00:29.542 --> 00:00:33.818
admissions each diagnosis has overall patient ID
does not belong in the

00:00:33.831 --> 00:00:38.384
grouping If the question asks how many admissions
each patient has for

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:44.381
each diagnosis then both columns are required When a
grouped query returns

00:00:44.395 --> 00:00:47.552
too many or too few rows inspect the GROUP BY list
first

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:49.934
and restate the intended grain in plain language
